      "summary": "O&M Newsletter, August 2026\nMaine Department of Environmental Protection sent this bulletin at 08/05/2026 04:12 PM EDT\nAUGUST 2026\nIn this issue:\nBreaking: Active Cyber Breaches Affecting Public Water Systems Demand Immediate Action.\nCISA Alert to Water and Wastewater Systems Regarding Cybersecurity Threats.\nStay Informed: Key Updates on Rulemaking for Chapters 595 and 579!\nState Laboratory Certification Required for In-House Testing of Nitrogen and Phosphorus Samples.\nEPA Announces WIFIA Application Fee Waiver for Small Communities.\nDMR-QA 2026 Update.\nTraining Highlights.\nFor Practice.\nBreaking: Active Cyber Breaches Affecting Public Water Systems Demand Immediate Action.\nThe US EPA, FBI, Cybersecurity & Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA), and Water Information Sharing & Analysis Center (WaterISAC) have held urgent briefings regarding\nactive and on-going cybersecurity breaches at dozens of Public Water Systems (PWSs) in at least seven states across the U.S.\nThe targeted PWSs range in size from small to large.\nMany wastewater systems use similar technology as found in the drinking water sector. A common symptom of these breaches includes a loss of PLC connectivity with devices. These incidents all involve vulnerabilities related to PLCs, as described in the\nIranian-Affiliated Cyber Actors Exploit Programmable Logic Controllers Across US Critical Infrastructure\nadvisory (PDF).\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) has information and guidance regarding malicious cyber actors targeting PLCs.\nMalicious Cyber Actors Targeting Water Sector Internet-Facing PLCs.pdf\nRestoring Access to a MicroLogix 1400 Controller - Password Unknown.pdf\n\"Malicious Cyber Actors Targeting Water and Wastewater Sector Internet-Facing Programmable Logic Controllers, Causing Operational Disruptions\" is a brief description of the current threat landscape pertaining to PLCs.\n\"Restoring Access to a MicroLogix\nTM\n1400 Controller When the Password is Unknown\" offers guidance on restoring acce",
      "summary_html": "<article>\n<div class=\"account_banner\">\n<div class=\"qs_banner\">\n<a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/dep/index.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">\n<img alt=\"Maine Department of Environmental Protection\" src=\"/system/images/39346/original/Department_of_Environmental_Protection.jpg?1387311240\"/>\n</a>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bulletin_display\" id=\"bulletin_content\">\n<h1 class=\"bulletin_subject\">O&amp;M Newsletter, August 2026</h1>\n<span class=\"dateline rs_skip\">Maine Department of Environmental Protection sent this bulletin at 08/05/2026 04:12 PM EDT</span>\n<div class=\"bulletin_header rs_skip\" id=\"bulletin_header\"></div>\n<div class=\"bulletin_body\" id=\"bulletin_body\"><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"gd_tbl_wrap\" width=\"100%\"><tr><td style=\"text-align: center; margin: 0; padding: 0; width: 100% !important\"><table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" id=\"gd_ab_main_tab\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 600px; text-align: left; margin: 20px auto;\" width=\"600\">\n<tr>\n<td data-govdstyle=\"all\" data-govdtitle=\"Masthead\" id=\"gd_ab_header\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; vertical-align: top; padding: 20px; border: none;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"600\">\n<img alt=\"O &amp; M Newsletter header\" class=\"govd_template_image\" height=\"119\" src=\"https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/MEDEP/2014/01/252375/omheader-working_original.jpg\" style=\"width: 600px; height: auto; border: 0px none;\" width=\"600\"/><img alt=\"EnviroNews banner: forest stream, lake cottage, landfill construction, autumn field, winter lakefront\" class=\"govd_template_image\" height=\"75\" src=\"https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/MEDEP/2014/01/250039/photos-for-division-wall-art1-original600_original.jpg\" style=\"width: 600px; height: auto; border: 0px none;\" width=\"600\"/>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-govdstyle=\"all\" data-govdtitle=\"Main body\" id=\"gd_ab_main_body\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; vertical-align: top; padding: 15px; border: 3px solid #000000;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"600\">\n<h3 align=\"right\" style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #0F2C50; text-align: right; margin: 3px 0 4px; padding: 0;\"><strong>AUGUST 2026</strong></h3>\n<h1 align=\"left\" class=\"govd_header\" style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #0F0101; text-align: left; margin: 0 0 5px; padding: 0;\">In this issue:</h1>\n<ul class=\"govd_toc\" style=\"font: 13px/1.5 Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"#link_3\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\">Breaking: Active Cyber Breaches Affecting Public Water Systems Demand Immediate Action.</a></li>\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"#link_4\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\">CISA Alert to Water and Wastewater Systems Regarding Cybersecurity Threats.</a></li>\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"#link_1389912064779\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\">Stay Informed: Key Updates on Rulemaking for Chapters 595 and 579!</a></li>\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"#link_1389912066563\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\">State Laboratory Certification Required for In-House Testing of Nitrogen and Phosphorus Samples.</a></li>\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"#link_1389912068132\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\">EPA Announces WIFIA Application Fee Waiver for Small Communities.</a></li>\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"#link_1389912070779\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\">DMR-QA 2026 Update.</a></li>\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"#link_1\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\">Training Highlights.</a></li>\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"#link_1389912072571\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\">For Practice.</a></li>\n</ul>\n<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"govd_hr\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; padding: 5px;\" width=\"100%\"><tr class=\"govd_hr_inner\"><td style=\"border-collapse: collapse; vertical-align: top;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"100%\"><hr/></td></tr></table>\n<h1 align=\"left\" class=\"govd_header\" style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #0F0101; text-align: left; margin: 0 0 5px; padding: 0;\"><a class=\"gd_anchor\" id=\"link_3\" name=\"link_3\" style=\"text-decoration: none; color: #1D5782;\">Breaking: Active Cyber Breaches Affecting Public Water Systems Demand Immediate Action.</a></h1>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"gd_combo_table\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-collapse: collapse; vertical-align: top;\" valign=\"top\">\n<img align=\"left\" alt=\"Cybersecurity\" class=\"govd_template_image\" height=\"140\" hspace=\"7\" src=\"https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/MEDEP/2026/08/14139209/cybersecurity_original.jfif\" style=\"width: 241px; height: auto; float: left; border: 0px none;\" width=\"241\"/>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.0em; color: #000000; font: 14px/1.5 arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The US EPA, FBI, Cybersecurity &amp; Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA), and Water Information Sharing &amp; Analysis Center (WaterISAC) have held urgent briefings regarding <strong>active and on-going cybersecurity breaches at dozens of Public Water Systems (PWSs) in at least seven states across the U.S.</strong> The targeted PWSs range in size from small to large.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.0em; color: #000000; font: 14px/1.5 arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Many wastewater systems use similar technology as found in the drinking water sector. A common symptom of these breaches includes a loss of PLC connectivity with devices. These incidents all involve vulnerabilities related to PLCs, as described in the <a href=\"https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fwww.ic3.gov%252FCSA%252F2026%252F260722.pdf%253Futm_medium%3Demail%2526utm_source%3Dgovdelivery%2F1%2F0101019faef2edac-3e92bc93-cf5c-4211-b881-4b32ea3acd8b-000000%2FmWkD1XTyVXy7YxvCQsyR61SmZK9JJOgrByTC70uvZYQ%3D452&amp;data=05%7C02%7CJudy.K.Bruenjes%40maine.gov%7C29f513ada2454265eb4e08deef06ae44%7C413fa8ab207d4b629bcdea1a8f2f864e%7C0%7C0%7C639211009155631389%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=LIiyk60tHQY6J5WYOaJrKFHezj3vYeVVvlUVOTzQqOg%3D&amp;reserved=0\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #3034E9;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Iranian-Affiliated Cyber Actors Exploit Programmable Logic Controllers Across US Critical Infrastructure Advisory\">Iranian-Affiliated Cyber Actors Exploit Programmable Logic Controllers Across US Critical Infrastructure</a> advisory (PDF).</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.0em; color: #000000; font: 14px/1.5 arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) has information and guidance regarding malicious cyber actors targeting PLCs.</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-position: inside; font: 13px/1.5 Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">\n<li style=\"color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><a href=\"https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fcontent.govdelivery.com%252Fattachments%252FMEHHS%252F2026%252F08%252F03%252Ffile_attachments%252F3